# What stays out of the repository, and why. Everything else is tracked, including the run records in results/,
# the report's figures and the built report PDF, because those cannot be recreated without the cluster time that
# produced them.

# Build outputs: rebuilt from src/ by scripts/build.sh or CMake on any machine.
/bin/
_build/
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Downloaded SNAP graphs: large, not ours to redistribute, and fetched again on the cluster by scripts/fetch_snap.sh.
data/

# PBS terminal output of the cluster jobs. The grader asks for no log files, and everything the report uses is in the
# run records under results/.
cluster/logs/

# Job scripts written from the plan by checks/run_plan.py pbs. They are regenerated from config/ on demand.
cluster/generated/

# The copy that cluster/ops/fetch.sh empties and refills on every fetch. The merged records are in results/<cluster>/.
results/.staging/

# Transcripts of the fake-cluster tests (cluster/ops/test_fake_cluster.sh). They are terminal output, rewritten by
# every test run, and no report number comes from them.
results/ops_tests/

# Terminal transcripts of the validation runs. The .json and .csv files next to them hold the same results and are
# what the report reads, and the grader asks for no terminal output.
results/validation/**/*.txt

# Draft figures drawn during development. The report uses only figures/*.pdf.
figures/dev/

# LaTeX log of the report build.
report/*.log

# ASCII copies of the appendix files, rewritten by scripts/make_report.sh from the sources on every build. The rest
# of report/generated/ (the values and tables) is tracked, because the tracked PDF depends on it and its diff shows
# which report numbers changed when new run records arrive.
report/generated/listing/

# macOS folder metadata.
.DS_Store
